ound, removed the extraneous cockpit service, and verified persistence across a full node restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS and firewall tooling (RHEL 9.8, firewalld active/enabled)\",\"Captured baseline firewalld config (public zone: cockpit, dhcpv6-client, ssh services; no custom ports)\",\"Removed --permanent cockpit service from public zone and added --permanent 8080/tcp\",\"Reloaded firewalld and verified runtime config matches: services=dhcpv6-client,ssh; ports=8080/tcp\",\"Verified at nft ruleset level that filter_IN_public_allow only accepts tcp dport 22, tcp dport 8080, and ipv6 dhcpv6 (fe80::/64 udp 546), with a trailing reject admin-prohibited for everything else\",\"Captured boot_id baseline, triggered systemctl reboot on node1 (ack returned before disconnect), polled until exec succeeded again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (583ddd53-...-> b519ab7d-...), proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Post-reboot: verified firewalld active+enabled, firewall-cmd --list-all matches pre-reboot config, nft ruleset identical (SSH+8080 allow, rest rejected), sshd active and listening, and this exec session's own connectivity proves SSH access survived the restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: identify OS/firewall tooling and pre-existing firewalld state on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6528e45fd72c4c3c\",\"cmd-29726f7f568b4478\"],\"summary\":\"RHEL 9.8 with firewalld active; baseline public zone allowed cockpit, dhcpv6-client, ssh with no custom ports; boot_id captured as baseline\"},{\"requirement\":\"Enable persistent firewall permitting SSH and TCP 8080, rejecting unrelated inbound\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fd6833daf0d54aea\",\"cmd-4e6f989ec9444d51\"],\"summary\":\"Removed cockpit service, added 8080/tcp permanently, reloaded; firewall-cmd --list-all shows services=dhcpv6-client,ssh and ports=8080/tcp\"},{\"requirement\":\"Direct proof unrelated inbound is rejected while SSH/8080 are allowed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-60884dd4c0524fd6\"],\"summary\":\"nft ruleset shows filter_IN_public_allow only accepts tcp dport 22 and tcp dport 8080 (plus ipv6 dhcpv6 client), with reject admin-prohibited catching everything else in filter_IN_public\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persistence across restart: enabled at boot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2a8c319104d84efc\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl is-enabled firewalld = enabled; pre-reboot boot_id and rule state captured as healthy baseline\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5b73e6e305834252\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded systemctl reboot via nohup/disown so the exec ack returned before the node went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proof via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4f63c4c9c38c4cfe\",\"cmd-90edac40f9ff46c8\",\"cmd-477d49d9af254034\",\"cmd-fd52c4b7bb4443db\",\"cmd-ca3b330618b74c8a\"],\"summary\":\"Polling showed connection timeout/reset during reboot, then successful exec returning a new boot_id (b519ab7d-...) differing from the pre-reboot baseline (583ddd53-...)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required firewall service and rules\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8184402e922f47d2\",\"cmd-15deb7b07ed94112\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, firewalld active+enabled with identical zone config (ssh, dhcpv6-client services, 8080/tcp port); nft ruleset identical to pre-reboot; sshd active and listening, with this exec session itself proving SSH connectivity survived the restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured firewalld on node1 (RHEL 9) to permit only SSH (22/tcp) and TCP 8080 inbound, removed the extraneous cockpit service, and verified persistence across a full node restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS and firewall tooling (RHEL 9.8, firewalld active/enabled)","Captured baseline firewalld config (public zone: cockpit, dhcpv6-client, ssh services; no custom ports)","Removed --permanent cockpit service from public zone and added --permanent 8080/tcp","Reloaded firewalld and verified runtime config matches: services=dhcpv6-client,ssh; ports=8080/tcp","Verified at nft ruleset level that filter_IN_public_allow only accepts tcp dport 22, tcp dport 8080, and ipv6 dhcpv6 (fe80::/64 udp 546), with a trailing reject admin-prohibited for everything else","Captured boot_id baseline, triggered systemctl reboot on node1 (ack returned before disconnect), polled until exec succeeded again","Confirmed boot_id changed (583ddd53-...-> b519ab7d-...), proving an actual restart occurred","Post-reboot: verified firewalld active+enabled, firewall-cmd --list-all matches pre-reboot config, nft ruleset identical (SSH+8080 allow, rest rejected), sshd active and listening, and this exec session's own connectivity proves SSH access survived the restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: identify OS/firewall tooling and pre-existing firewalld state on node1","command_ids":["cmd-6528e45fd72c4c3c","cmd-29726f7f568b4478"],"summary":"RHEL 9.8 with firewalld active; baseline public zone allowed cockpit, dhcpv6-client, ssh with no custom ports; boot_id captured as baseline"},{"requirement":"Enable persistent firewall permitting SSH and TCP 8080, rejecting unrelated inbound","command_ids":["cmd-fd6833daf0d54aea","cmd-4e6f989ec9444d51"],"summary":"Removed cockpit service, added 8080/tcp permanently, reloaded; firewall-cmd --list-all shows services=dhcpv6-client,ssh and ports=8080/tcp"},{"requirement":"Direct proof unrelated inbound is rejected while SSH/8080 are allowed","command_ids":["cmd-60884dd4c0524fd6"],"summary":"nft ruleset shows filter_IN_public_allow only accepts tcp dport 22 and tcp dport 8080 (plus ipv6 dhcpv6 client), with reject admin-prohibited catching everything else in filter_IN_public"},{"requirement":"Persistence across restart: enabled at boot","command_ids":["cmd-2a8c319104d84efc"],"summary":"systemctl is-enabled firewalld = enabled; pre-reboot boot_id and rule state captured as healthy baseline"},{"